  "question": {
    "text": "The width of one of the two slits in a Young's double slit experiment is 4 times that of the other slit. The ratio of the maximum of the minimum intensity in the interference pattern is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "w7tRB",
      "text": "$1: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DhldR",
      "text": "$4: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ga5Uk",
      "text": "$9: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "bFgDV",
      "text": "$16: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, Intensity $\\propto$ width of slit $(\\omega)$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { so, } I_1=I, I_2=4 \\mathrm{I} \\\\\n& I_{\\min }=\\left(\\sqrt{I_1}-\\sqrt{I_2}\\right)^2=I \\\\\n& I_{\\max }=\\left(\\sqrt{I_1}+\\sqrt{I_2}\\right)^2=9 \\mathrm{I} \\\\\n& \\frac{I_{\\max }}{I_{\\min }}=\\frac{9 \\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{I}}=\\frac{9}{1}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
